# Functional programming

Read `.docs/CODE_STANDARDS.md` §9 before editing `lib/`, `convex/`, or data-transform logic.

## Required

- Pure functions for transforms; no mutation — return new values
- `map` / `filter` / `reduce` over `for` loops for collection transforms
- `Result<T, E>` from `@/lib/fp` for fallible lib/convex logic — not bare `try/catch` in business logic
- `tryCatch` / `tryCatchAsync` to wrap fallible sync/async work — prefer over bare `try/catch` everywhere except inside `@/lib/fp` itself
- `tryCatchAsyncWithMessage` at UI/async boundaries that need a user-facing fallback string
- `pipe` when chaining >=3 pure steps

## Error handling pattern

```typescript
// lib/convex — return Result
export function validateLogMealInput(args): Result<void, MealPlanError> { ... }

// async boundary — tryCatchAsyncWithMessage + explicit branch
const result = await tryCatchAsyncWithMessage(
  () => mutation(args),
  FALLBACK_ERROR,
);
if (result.ok) onSuccess();
else onError(result.error);

// sync I/O — tryCatch + getOrElseResult
const value = getOrElseResult(
  tryCatch(() => JSON.parse(raw), () => new Error("invalid")),
  {},
);
```

## Boundaries (unwrap once)

- Convex mutation/query handlers — call `assert*` helpers or branch on `Result`
- React event handlers / hooks — use `tryCatchAsyncWithMessage`, not bare `try/catch`

## Reference

- Utilities: `@/lib/fp` (`tryCatch`, `tryCatchAsync`, `tryCatchAsyncWithMessage`, `pipe`, `Result`)
- Golden paths:
  - `lib/logMealValidation.ts` — `validateLogMealInput`, `assertLogMealInput`
  - `src/components/week-plan/useDebouncedSectionSave.ts` — `tryCatchAsyncWithMessage` in commit
